   "fen": "2r1r1k1/pp1bppbp/2np2p1/4q2n/2P1P3/1NN1BP2/PP1Q2P1/1K1R1B1R w - - 2 15",
   "line": [
    "Qe5"
   ],
   "spoken": "A crucial habit: a move that failed a moment ago doesn't stay refused forever. Because the queen has repositioned to a vulnerable central square, the whole picture has changed — the same g4 idea is worth a fresh look.",
   "kind": "plan"
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 403,
   "fen": "2r1r1k1/pp1bppbp/2np2p1/4q2n/2P1P1P1/1NN1BP2/PP1Q4/1K1R1B1R b - - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "g4"
   ],
   "spoken": "And now it works: after g4 chases the knight to g3, a bishop drops to f4 forking the queen and the knight at once. It's a semi-fake fork — the knight can grab on f1 and hit the queen back — but that never mattered, because the real aim was only to remove the knight and clear the road.",
   "kind": "tactic"
  },
  {
   "ply": 31,
   "t": 409.5,
   "fen": "2r1r1k1/pp1bppbp/2np2p1/4q3/2P1PBP1/1NN2Pn1/PP1Q4/1K1R1B1R b - - 2 16",
   "line": [
    "Ng3",
